	"*Our engineers say they are going to need time to decipher and extract the Allies' military weapon data."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL08
	"*You need to defend the science facility against Allied attempts to recapture or attack. They will stop at nothing to reclaim the facility."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL09
	"*Commander, remember to occupy the islands to the east. Their Ore Mines will fund your efforts."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL10
	"*The Allied Tech Inhibitor is denying the use of our full military arsenal. Take it out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL11
	"*Commander, you are authorized to use our Twinblade combat gunships. They are powerful and versatile."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL12
	"*The Tech Inhibitor is destroyed. You have regained access to additional technology."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL13
	"*Commander, we are downloading data on new Allied weapons technology. You must defend the science facility until we have that data."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL14
	"*The Allies have recaptured the facility! Quickly, you must capture it again!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL15
	"*You have recaptured the facility. Do not let it fall into Allied hands."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL16
	"*Commander, your forces lie in ruin. Mission Aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL17
	"*Your Co-Commander's base has been utterly destroyed. Mission Aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL18
	"*Commander, the data has been encrypted and is of no use. Mission Aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS05_SOVIETINTEL19
	"*The Allies are preparing to retaliate with air power. You are now authorized to build our own MiG Fighters to repel them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_COOLEG01
	"*All right, I'll take the base to the east."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_COOLEG02
	"*Western Allied base? No problem. Consider it dead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_COOLEG03
	"*Why would they build in somewhere so inaccessible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_COOLEG04
	"*Best not wait around for that thing to fire. We'd better take it down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_COOLEG05
	"*Burn, you old fool! You had this coming!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_COOLEG06
	"*Oh, it's that guy? I've been waiting to wipe that smirk off his face for years. Let's do this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL01
	"*The last major Allied target in Europe is the Von Esling Airbase. Destroying this base will effectively free the last of European lands from Allied control."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL02
	"*Your objective is simple:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL03
	"*Locate the Von Esling Airbase and destroy it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL04
	"*Due to the significance of this operation, General Krukov will once again be on site to supervise."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL05
	"*Best of luck, Commander - This is a treacherous place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL06
	"*The Premier has retaken command. He has prioritized a new objective of high authority."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL07
	"*Your forces are to eliminate General Krukov."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL08
	"*The Allied Air Base must still be destroyed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL09
	"*The Premier expects your compliance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL10
	"*Von Esling airbase is alerted to our presence. Please proceed with caution."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL11
	"*General Krukov has arrived to supervise this battle personally."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL12
	"*The Premier has spoken. Your new target is Krukov."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL13
	"*The Allies have a Proton Collider in the vicinity. You must find a way to destroy it before it can fire."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL14
	"*To support you in your goal, the Premier has provided you a new Soviet superweapons - the Vacuum Imploder."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL15
	"*Krukov's army has sworn allegiance to you, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL16
	"*Krukov's forces have sworn allegiance to your CoCommander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL17
	"*The Allies' Von Esling airbase has been detected. It must be destroyed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL18
	"*Capture the Oil Derricks in order to secure additional income for this mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL19
	"*The Premier has authorized you to construct Kirov Airships."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL20
	"*Krukov has been branded a traitor. Your priority is to eliminate him."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL21
	"*An expansion base will cement our grip on this battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL22
	"*It appears there is no land or sea access to this branch of the Allies' base. You must find another way to attack it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL23
	"*Your Co-Commander has been defeated. Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS06_SOVIETINTEL24
	"*Your base of operations is in ruin. Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_COMOSK01
	"*So this is our army for taking out the Emperor?! That's it?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_COMOSK02
	"*They're coming out of the woodwork it seems. Good..."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_COMOSK03
	"*Is that the emperor? If only I could kill him with my own hands."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_COMOSK04
	"*Our revenge is sweet, wouldn't you say, commander?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL01
	"*The Premier has ordered the assassination of the Emperor of the Rising Sun. Here is what you must do:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL02
	"*Assault the Emperor Yoshiro's palace grounds."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL03
	"*Eliminate Emperor Yoshiro. Make certain the Emperor does not escape."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL04
	"*Your forces have already begun their air drops into the Imperial Palace. Good luck to you in this operation."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL05
	"*The Empire of the Rising Sun's frontline commanders have assembled to protect their Emperor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL06
	"*The Premier has called for you to eliminate them along with the Emperor himself."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL07
	"*Invasion Force inbound."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL08
	"*Castle grounds crawl with Imperial guards. Sneak past patrols to the garden to search for the Emperor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL09
	"*Contact has been lost with landing party. The mission is a failure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL10
	"*Distraction needed to draw troops away from garden."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL11
	"*Keep moving toward the Emperor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL12
	"*MCV's inbound. Use to construct new base and take battle to hated enemies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL13
	"*Japanese commanders are protected by substantial defenses. Friends at the Kremlin have sent plans for Kirov. Use to rain down death on enemies of glorious revolution."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL14
	"*You now have access to Apocalpse Tanks- the toughest armor in the world."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL15
	"*The Premier has authorized use of Vacuum Bomb. Construct Vacuum Imploder building to use."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL16
	"*All our forces have been destroyed. Mission failure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL17
	"*With foolish Japanese commanders dead, you are free to focus attack on Emperor's Palace. Bring down this enclave of the entrenched bourgeoisie"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL18
	"*The Emperor is inside of that armor- eliminate him."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL19
	"*Despite the loss of our initial forces, the distraction allowed our MCVs to land nearby. Use our Apocalypse Tanks and construct a base to exact revenge on this place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS07_SOVIETINTEL20
	"*The path to the Emperor is clear. Finish him at once."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_ALLIEDSOLDIER01
	"Good afternoon, friend. Are you here to escort us to our meeting with the Premier?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_ALLIEDSOLDIER02
	"It's a setup! Retreat, retreat!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_ALLIEDSOLDIER03
	"What the--they've double-crossed us! Open fire!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_ALLIEDSOLDIER04
	"You cheating commie scum. Wait'll Allied high command gets wind of this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN01
	"*I just love these kinds of missions. But I wonder…  Are we supposed to be the cheese or the trap?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN02
	"*They have the island, but they have left themselves no place to run."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN03
	"*Well played! They didn't stand a chance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN04
	"*We did it! The Soviet people will be safer now, without that maniac."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN05
	"*Do you require assistance, Commander?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN06
	"*Tesla Tanks, weaponized Moai heads... A volcano fortress... Such madness."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_COZHAN07
	"*Brother against brother... May we end this madness quickly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL01
	"*The Allies are en route from the southeast, expecting to negotiate a treaty."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL02
	"*However, your task is to destroy them, therefore you must draw first blood. Here is what you must do:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL03
	"*Prepare an assault against the Allied forces coming to meet with the Premier."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL04
	"*Do not strike until you have the signal."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL05
	"*Standby for further orders from the Premier."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL06
	"*Good fortune to you in battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL07
	"*Commander, your mission has changed. The Premier is your new target, and you are his new target."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL08
	"*You must eliminate the Premier."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL09
	"*His fortress may be vulnerable to a direct attack, though forces loyal to the Premier will stand in your way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL10
	"*Be especially mindful of the Premier's experimental Tesla Tanks. Even now, our satellites show that he is mobilizing them against your position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL11
	"* The Allied Emissary's naval fleet is arriving soon. Build up sizeable force."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL12
	"*Wait for emissary to reach docks before surrounding him.  We don't want the fool to escape."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL13
	"*The Premier is attempting to target your base with a super weapon."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL14
	"*The Premier's super weapon is now firing. We cannot win now. Mission fail."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL15
	"*It is done…let us focus on Premier's secret volcano fortress."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL16
	"*Five minutes remaining."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL17
	"*One minute remaining."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL18
	"*Thirty seconds remaining."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL19
	"*Ten seconds remaining."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL20
	"*Five."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL21
	"*Four."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL22
	"*Three."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL23
	"*Two."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL24
	"*One."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL25
	"*The Allies have escaped- your mission is failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL26
	"*The Allied Emissary got away. Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL27
	"*The emissary will be arriving by sea. Be prepared to strike from the air or the waters."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL28
	"*Enemy force composition not yet known. Observe the Allied forces carefully as they arrive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL29
	"*The emissary has arrived. We are making final confirmations that he is on board before giving the order to attack. Standby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL30
	"*Cleared to engage. Attack the Allies now. Destroy the emissary and all of his forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL31
	"*Be advised: The allies have established a base to the west on a small island."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL32
	"*Commander, we have located several ore mines to the north of your position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL33
	"*The Premier intends to eliminate us all with his new superweapon. Please hurry, commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL34
	"*Beware of the enemy Tesla Tanks. These experimental forces appear to have very few vulnerabilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL35
	"*The Premier's stronghold appears to have been built into the volcano itself."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL36
	"*The fortress is well defended. However, destroying three key support structures should disable it completely."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL37
	"*One fortress structure down. Two remain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETINTEL38
	"*Two fortress structures eliminated. One remains."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS08_SOVIETSOLDIER01
	"I am afraid not, \"my friend.\" Comrades! Attack now!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_COMOSK01
	"*Let's take these terror drones out for a little walk!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_COMOSK02
	"*Yes! Let's take her down!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_COMOSK03
	"*Where did you get these Tesla Tanks from anyway...?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_COMOSK04
	"*That she-wolf put up a fight, I'll give her that."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_COMOSK05
	"*Ah, they still want to fight! All the more to kill!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL01
	"*This could be the final battle plan, Commander. Our targets are the Allied military fortress in New York City, as well as the Statue Liberty."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL02
	"*The Allies will be on high alert, relying on any forces they can muster- take caution when moving in on a base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL03
	"*You must topple the symbol of their tyranny: The Statue of Liberty."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL04
	"*With this symbolic gesture, the Allies will have no choice but to submit to the Soviet revolution. Good luck, Comrade."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL05
	"*The city is heavily fortified. This will require a superior strategy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL06
	"*We've infiltrated small force via Ellis Island.  Use them to recover captured MCV's"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL07
	"*Commander, it seems Fort Bradley has upgraded alert status."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL08
	"*Commander, the Liberty Park garrison has upgraded their Alert Status."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL09
	"*Commander, our forces are picking up Chronosphere energy signatures near the Statue of Liberty!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL10
	"*You'll each need engineer to get MCV up and running Commander. Do NOT waste them all!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL11
	"*Capturing Allied Technology is all good and well, Commander, but do NOT forget you will need Engineer to get MCVs working as intended."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL12
	"*Engineer is essential."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL13
	"*Fort Bradley’s ore-refining operations offline."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL14
	"*Your invasion force is imminent. Please standby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL15
	"*Your invasion force has arrived."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL16
	"*An allied attack is incoming."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL17
	"*Alert: Chronosphere anomalies detected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL18
	"*Alert: Allied paradrop incoming."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL19
	"*Set up an outpost near Fort Bradley's vacated ore mines if you require additional resources."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL20
	"*Our Twinblades can transport infantry and vehicle reinforcements across the river."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS09_SOVIETINTEL21
	"*Plans for the Premier's ultimate weapon, the Vacuum Imploder, are now available to you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_AKULASUB
	"*Akula Subs excel at quickly destroying enemy ships with their torpedoes. They must surface to fire, but are invulnerable to most attacks while submerged.  Their special ability is to launch ultratorpedoes, which are devastating unguided warheads that rapidly accelerate straight ahead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_APOCALYPSETANK
	"*Apocalypse Tanks can easily take on other vehicles with their powerful main guns, and can crush most anything under their massive treads.  Their special ability is a magnetic harpoon, which can draw enemy vehicles in for the kill."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_BULLFROG
	"*Bullfrogs are amphibious anti-aircraft troop transports. Their flak cannons can quickly destroy enemy aircraft.  The only means for passengers to exit a Bullfrog is via the \"man cannon\", which can be used to launch infantry behind enemy lines."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_CONSCRIPT
	"*Conscripts are the Union's mainline anti-infantry forces. They are not well-trained but can be effective in numbers.  They carry assault rifles and can also switch to using Molotov cocktails, which are more effective against structures, including garrisons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_DREADNOUGHT
	"*Dreadnoughts are powerful long-range bombardment ships armed with multiple rocket launchers. They can destroy any surface target in moments.  Their special ability makes them fire even more rapidly, although forcing the weapons systems to do this gradually causes internal damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_ENGINEER
	"*Combat Engineers can capture neutral or enemy structures both on land or at sea, or repair your damaged structures. They carry basic revolvers for self-defense.  Their special ability is to build a Battle Bunker, which can be garrisoned by other infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_FLAKTROOPER
	"*Flak Troopers are convicts forced to carry out their sentence by fighting with heavy weapons on the front lines. They are most effective against aircraft.  They can switch to using magnetic mines that work well against vehicles. These mines will also detonate should a vehicle crush the Flak Trooper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_HAMMERTANK
	"*Hammer Tanks are effective against most vehicles and structures. Further, they can crush infantry under their treads.  Instead of using their main gun, they can switch to using the Leech Beam, which absorbs enemy armor. The beam can steal enemy weapons as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_KIROV
	"*Kirov Airships are flying heavy bombers. Nothing on the ground can withstand their bombs. Kirovs are slow but highly durable.  Their special ability provides them with a burst of speed using a chemical process that slowly causes them to take damage. Therefore it must be used sparingly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_MCV
	"*Mobile Construction Vehicles are amphibious mobile bases. They are critical to battlefield operations, even though they have no weapons of their own.  Once unpacked into Construction Yards, they can build all facilities authorized by the Soviet war council. They must be defended by any means necessary."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_MIGFIGHTER
	"*MiG Fighters are specialized air-superiority jets, designed purely for intercepting groups of enemy aircraft.  They carry a limited supply of ammunition and must occasionally rearm at an Airbase. They have a special ability to rapidly return to base if needed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_NATASHA
	"*Natasha is the Union's greatest sniper-commando, whose rifle can kill several infantry in one shot. She may also call in airstrikes against other targets.  Her special ability is to snipe pilots cleanly in their vehicles, such that the vehicles can then be captured. Natasha is equally effective on land or at sea."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_ORECOLLECTOR
	"*Ore Collectors automatically gather resources essential to fueling the Soviet War Machine. These amphibious vehicles must be protected at all costs.  Their special ability is to deploy reactive armor, which makes them highly resistant to enemy attacks. Note they cannot gather resources in this state."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_SICKLE
	"*Sickles are fast-moving anti-personnel vehicles armed with three independently-firing machine guns.  Their special ability lets them leap long distances, or even onto enemy infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_SPUTNIK
	"*Sputniks are defenseless vehicles that offer an economical alternative to Mobile Construction Vehicles when it becomes necessary to expand.  These amphibious units may convert to an Outpost almost anywhere, allowing other Soviet structures to be built nearby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_STINGRAY
	"*Stingrays are experimental strike craft fitted with Tesla weapons that are effective against most targets. Stingrays are amphibious, though slower-moving on land.  Their special ability is the Tesla Surge, which shoots lightning in all directions while briefly immobilizing the unit. It only works on water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TERRORDRONE
	"*Terror Drones are amphibious robots that can kill enemy infantry or tear into vehicles and dismantle them from the inside. Once infected, the vehicle must be repaired, or else it will be destroyed. Terror Drones can switch to using an electro-stasis ray that shuts down vehicle locomotors, preventing them from moving."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TESLATANK
	"*Tesla Tanks are experimental vehicles whose dual Tesla coil weapons are more powerful than most any conventional weapon.  Like Tesla Troopers, Tesla Tanks may switch to using electromagnetic disrupters that disable enemy vehicles nearby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TESLATROOPER
	"*Tesla Troopers are heavy infantry armed with electrifying weapons effective against most targets. They are too big to be crushed by most tanks.  Their special ability is to switch to using electromagnetic disrupters that automatically disable enemy vehicles in the vicinity."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TWINBLADE
	"*Twinblades are anti-surface combat helicopters armed with machine guns and rockets.  In addition to their powerful weapons, Twinblades function as transports, and can ferry infantry or some vehicles across the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_V4ROCKETLNCHR
	"*V4 Rocket Launchers are long-range artillery pieces whose rockets can quickly destroy most any unit or structure, if they hit.  Their special ability is to fire multiwarheads that split up in flight, causing widespread damage. Note V4s cannot defend themselves up close."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_WARBEAR
	"*War Bears are trained for scouting by land and sea, as well as anti-infantry combat. Their mauling attack is lethal against most infantry.  Their special ability is an amplified roar that causes paralysis in enemy infantry within earshot. War Bears also detect disguised enemy units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN01
	"*Oy, welcome to Command & Conquer Red Alert 3."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN02
	"*I'm an Allied Guardian Tank, and these prats and I are here to tell you about how we think you should be doing your job. Sir."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN03
	"*Coh, blimey…right, OK... To move your camera around the battlefield, just hold down the right mouse button and slide your mouse around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN04
	"*Coh, blimey…right, OK... To move your camera around the battlefield, just move your left stick around. Try moving your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN05
	"*Easy enough."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN06
	"*Now, to rotate the camera, hold down the middle mouse button and move the mouse around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN07
	"*Now, to rotate the camera, move the right stick left or right."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN08
	"*To zoom the camera in and out, simply slide your mouse wheel."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN09
	"*To zoom the camera in and out, simply move the right stick up or down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN10
	"*As you go about fussing with the camera, sir, remember you can always click the middle mouse button to reset the viewing angle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN11
	"*As you go about fussing with the camera, sir, remember you can always click the Right Stick button to reset the viewing angle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN12
	"*Right proper, you have. Objectives, as you might have surmised, are special goals you need to accomplish in order to progress through the campaigns."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN13
	"*If at any time you're not sure what in blazes you're supposed to be doing, hit the Escape key to pay a visit to the mission menu. It'll list all your current objectives."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN14
	"*If at any time you're not sure what in blazes you're supposed to be doing, hit the START button to pay a visit to the mission menu. It'll list all your current objectives."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN15
	"*Right. To select a unit, just left-click on it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN16
	"*Right. To select a unit, just move your cursor over it and press the A button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN17
	"*Nice. He's definitely one of ours, sir."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN18
	"*I was getting to that."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN19
	"*To move your units, whilst having them selected, click the right mouse button on any open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN20
	"*To move your units, whilst having them selected, press the A button with your cursor over the desired destination."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN21
	"*Erm... Right, so, to issue an Attack Order to your units, whilst having them selected, put your cursor over a target and click the right mouse button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN22
	"*Erm... Right, so, to issue an Attack Order to your units, whilst having them selected, put your cursor over a target and press A."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN23
	"*Bloody robots."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN24
	"*Now, in addition to issuing attack commands on specific targets, you can have your units move and attack any enemies along the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN25
	"*Now that's a fine job you did there, Commander! You now know how to move around the battlefield as well as how to make your forces shoot their enemies dead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER01
	"*Yes. We have temporarily called a truce to make sure you do not send us to our deaths needlessly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER02
	"*To begin with, we will tell you how to move your viewpoint around the battlefield and how to command your units, including the best ones such as me, the Soviet Hammer Tank!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER03
	"*Just look this body compared with the teeny little Japanese tank to my left."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER04
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER05
	"*You may also move your cursor to the far edges of the screen!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER06
	"*My goodness, commander! You have completed your first objective!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER07
	"*Good! Now that you have an idea for how to move around the battlefield, let's move on to controlling your units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER08
	"*Here come some of our hated enemies now!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER09
	"*You may also hold down the left mouse button and drag your mouse. This will create a selection box. Any units inside the selection box will be selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER10
	"*You may also press and hold the A button for an expanded selection cursor. Any units you sweep with the cursor will be selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER11
	"*Easier still, just tap the X button to select all your combat units onscreen. Or double-tap X to select all combat units on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER12
	"*And if you want more units added to your selection, hold down the Shift key and drag a selection box around those units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER13
	"*And if you want more units added to your selection, hold down the Left Bumper while selecting."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER14
	"*OK, now that we've reminded you how to select units, you’ll need to move them around the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER15
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER16
	"*See? They obey you without question!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER17
	"*They seem so real..."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER18
	"*Observe that you can distinguish your forces from the robots based on the colored blips in the Radar in the upper-right corner of your battlefield control display."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER19
	"*The color of the blips refers to the color of the different sides involved in a battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER20
	"*Notice that as you move your mouse cursor over those dummies, it changes to an attack cursor!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER21
	"*So long you stupid robots!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER22
	"*To issue an Attack-Move command, while having your units selected, just press the A key and right-click on any open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER23
	"*You can issue Attack-Move orders on the Radar as well!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER24
	"*To issue an Attack-Move command, while having your units selected, just double-tap the A button on any open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER25
	"*You can also use an Assault-Move command by double-tapping and holding button A with forces selected. Then, use the wider reticle to paint enemy targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER26
	"*You can also issue an Assault-Move command by pressing and holding button A with forces selected. Then use the  wider reticle to paint enemy targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER27
	"*Once you've painted some targets, release button A and your forces will automatically attack those targets to the best of their ability."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER28
	"*See you there!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI01
	"*Shut up!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI02
	"*Please excuse him, sir. Let us begin."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI03
	"*Try moving your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI04
	"*Try rotating your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI05
	"*Try zooming your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI06
	"*In general, objectives will be labeled using special markers out on the battlefield. Follow the onscreen indicators to get to them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI07
	"*Try selecting one of these Allied Peacekeepers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI08
	"*Try moving your units to the designated area up ahead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI09
	"*Notice, Commander, how the darkened area of the battlefield revealed itself as your forces drew near."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI10
	"*This darkened area is the Fog of War, and represents parts of the battlefield that may be hiding enemy troop movements."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI11
	"*Be careful when venturing into unseen areas, and use your scouts to survey the terrain before committing your forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI12
	"*Now, up ahead are some dummy targets that you're going to destroy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI13
	"*They resemble real-life Soviet Conscripts, but I assure you they are merely robots we created for this exercise."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI14
	"*See how foolishly they behave?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI15
	"*If you encounter different-colored blips as you clear the Fog of War, those are likely enemy forces. So be prepared."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI16
	"*If you need to take a closer look at your Radar, you can always use Radar Mode."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI17
	"*To activate Radar Mode, pull and hold the Right Trigger. Try this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI18
	"*To activate Radar Mode, pull and hold the Left Trigger. Try this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI19
	"*Hai, that is it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI20
	"*In Radar Mode, you may navigate the battlefield much more quickly using the Left Stick."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI21
	"*You may also use the Right Stick to move your cursor independently of your view. This allows you to quickly order your forces anywhere on the map."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI22
	"*Destroy all the target dummies in the area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI23
	"*Now, look there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI24
	"*We need you to lead us to that strategic point, yet many robots stand in the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI25
	"*If you please, issue an Attack-Move order to the strategic point. You have the command. Lead us to victory!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI26
	"*Indeed. We suggest you move on to the next lesson on building a military base for further instruction on properly commanding an army."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN01
	"*Good to have you, Commander. In this mission, we'll be reminding you all about constructing a base for each of the factions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN02
	"*We'll start with the Allies for obvious reasons. First things first, though."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN03
	"*On the right side of the screen is the Sidebar, which is where you manage all your base construction and unit production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN04
	"*You need to know about the Command Menu. Pull and hold the Left Trigger to bring up the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN05
	"*You need to know about the Command Menu. Pull and hold the Right Trigger to bring up the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN06
	"*The Command Menu lets you do everything from build units and structures to use your units' special abilities, and much more."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN07
	"*It's arranged like the face of a clock. You can make selections along the periphery by moving the Left Stick and pressing button A to confirm."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN08
	"*In general, you can drill deeper or confirm selections in the Command Menu with button A, or go back up or cancel selections with button B."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN09
	"*Go ahead and get comfortable using this thing. It lets you manage all your forces and production no matter where you're focusing your attention in battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN10
	"*Best remember to use the F hotkey as a shortcut to your units' special abilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN11
	"*Best remember there's a shortcut for using your units' special abilities. Just hold the Right Bumper with units selected, then press the X button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN12
	"*Bear in mind that there may be impassable areas of the map where you're not allowed to place down your structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN13
	"*When you try to place a structure down over impassable or un-buildable terrain, red cells will appear on the build grid indicating that you're unable to place a structure there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN14
	"*That's the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN15
	"*As the name suggests, a Power Plant provides your base with power. All your structures, with the exception of your Power Plant and Construction Yard, use power."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN16
	"*You can tell how much power you've got to spare by glancing at the power meter next to your Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN17
	"*It's important to understand the consequences of a low-power situation."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN18
	"*While in Low Power, your units and structures will build at a reduced speed, and your base defenses won't work, so it's always good to have plenty of power as you build up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN19
	"*When you place your Ore Refinery, you get a Prospector as part of the deal, and he'll go about collecting ore for you automatically."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN20
	"*Pro tip, friend: If by some freak accident, one of your Prospectors or Ore Collectors is destroyed, you can always build another from your Ore Refineries."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN21
	"*Just select the Ore Refinery and you'll see it can build another resource vehicle as its special ability."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN22
	"*As long as your Ore Refinery is close to a mine, you only need one vehicle gathering from it, so don't waste credits making more of those little tykes than you need."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN23
	"*You now have power and an economy set up. You’re ready to start training units for the fight. From your Production Tab, go ahead and build a Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN24
	"*You now have power and an economy set up. You’re ready to start training units for the fight. Go ahead and open up the Command Menu and build a Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN25
	"*Remember to place it down by selecting its icon, then left-clicking on open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN26
	"*Remember to place it down by opening the Command Menu once it's built, pressing A to select it, then pressing A again on open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN27
	"*Incidentally, you can rotate the face of a structure you're about to plop down by holding down the left mouse button and moving the mouse around. Let go of the button when ready."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN28
	"*Incidentally, you can rotate the facing of a structure you're about to plop down by holding down the A button and moving the left stick around. Let the button go when ready."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN29
	"*Try holding the Shift key to queue up five of those blokes at a time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN30
	"*You can set a different rally point for them by selecting the structure and right-clicking some other place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN31
	"*All three factions produce units in the same way, from the respective tabs in the sidebar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN32
	"*You can set a different rally point for them by selecting the structure, moving your cursor to the desired location, and pressing button A."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN33
	"*All three factions produce units in the same way, from the respective queues in the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN34
	"*By the by, many of your structures aren’t restricted to being built on land. You can set 'em up on water as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN35
	"*If you build another Power Plant, try placing it out in the drink. It doesn't cost you any extra and most ground units won't be able to get to it that way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN36
	"*Yeah, that's it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN37
	"*Also, bear in mind that the Allies' Technology Level is local to their Construction Yards or Command Hubs."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN38
	"*That means not all your production structures on the battlefield may offer you the same construction options."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN39
	"*You can upgrade your Construction Yard or your Command Hub by clicking the Heightened Clearance button with one of these structures selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN40
	"*You can upgrade your Construction Yard or your Command Hub by selecting them, opening the Command Menu, and selecting the Heightened Clearance button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN41
	"*Try requesting Heightened Clearance on both your ConYard and your Command Hub now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN42
	"*That's it. Now the other."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN43
	"*There it is."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN44
	"*Heightened Clearance costs you, and there's even a higher clearance level after that."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN45
	"*You need to decide when and where to request better tech when commanding the Allies, else things may turn rotten."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN46
	"*Notice how the structure is hastily being thrown together in the field."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN47
	"*While it's building up, it's vulnerable to enemy attack, so be cautious when placing your structures. All Soviet structures build up in this way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN48
	"*Oy, aren't you forgetting something?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN49
	"*Haha, keep fussing with the Imperial build system if you want, and when you're all set, select me and we'll wrap up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN50
	"*Well, that concludes the lesson on base-building. Don't worry, the other ones will be shorter. Mostly. Let's shove off, lads."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN51
	"*Commander, see you then."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER01
	"*Here we have one of the hated Allied Mobile Construction Vehicles. The MCV will unpack into a Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER02
	"*To unpack it, select it, then click on its special ability button at the bottom right of your screen. Go on, don't be shy!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER03
	"*To unpack it, select it, then use its Unpack special ability by bringing up the Command Menu and pressing the A button. Go on, don't be shy!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER04
	"*Very fancy, no?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER05
	"*In general, special abilities are executed with the left mouse button, or canceled with the right mouse button. However, the right mouse button is used for basic orders."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER06
	"*In general, special abilities are executed with the A button, or canceled with the B button. The B button is also used to deselect units or structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER07
	"*Now that your MCV has unpacked into a Construction Yard, you should have some new construction options available to you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER08
	"*To access your production structures build queue, select the ConYard or click on the Production Tab that's flashing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER09
	"*To access your production structures build queue, select the ConYard and open the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER10
	"*Alternatively, if you don't have anything selected, open the Command Menu and drill down to your Production Structures in the 12 o'clock position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER11
	"*Whoa, look at what we have here! Looks like you have access to build a Power Plant!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER12
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER13
	"*The next thing you'll need to get base humming along is an Ore Refinery."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER14
	"*This structure comes with a free Prospector vehicle, which will collect ore from that nearby Ore Mine."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER15
	"*To build your Ore Refinery, select the Production Tab and select the Ore Refinery button, just as you did with the Power Plant."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER16
	"*To build your Ore Refinery, open the Command Menu, navigate to your Production Structures, and press the Ore Refinery Button, just as you did with the Power Plant."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER17
	"*Now that construction is complete, click the Ore Refinery button and consider where to place it on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER18
	"*Now that construction is complete, open the Command Menu and select the Ore Refinery and consider where to place it on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER19
	"*While you're able to place your Refinery anywhere on open terrain, the optimal location is just in front of an Ore Mine."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER20
	"*You'll see those spots ghosted on the terrain. As you move your cursor over those spots, your structure preview should snap to the optimal position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER21
	"*Then, just click to place your Ore Refinery and you're set!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER22
	"*Then, just press the A button to place your Ore Refinery and you're set!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER23
	"*I always wonder, though... how come the mightiest nations in the world need to collect ore while killing each other? I mean, what is even in that stuff?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER24
	"*Ow!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER25
	"*Now that you have a Boot Camp, you’re able to train some infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER26
	"*To do this, you may select either your Boot Camp or the Infantry Tab under your Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER27
	"*To do this, you may select either your Boot Camp and open the Command Menu, or navigate to your Infantry Queues in the 2 o'clock position in the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER28
	"*This will bring up the available units you’re able to train. Let’s train some of the so-called \"Peacekeepers.\""
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER29
	"*Select the Peacekeeper button to start training one."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER30
	"*You may queue up multiple Peacekeepers by continuing to select on his portrait."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER31
	"*Yes. Also, should you ever have need to run away like a little girl, you may pack up your ConYard, then unpack it on the water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER32
	"*The Boot Camp and Armor Facility are the only Allied structures you may not place on the water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER33
	"*Your Seaport, on the other hand, is the only structure you may not build on land."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER34
	"*Ow! What was that for?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER35
	"*Just like the Allies, however, you can pause and cancel a structure's build-up by right-clicking on its button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER36
	"*Just like the Allies, however, you can pause and cancel a structure's build-up by navigating to that structure in the Command Menu and using the B button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER37
	"*And of course, your Soviet structures may be placed at sea -- with the exceptions of the Barracks and War Factory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER38
	"*Nyet! At least... not anymore."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER39
	"*Commander, one truly unique Soviet structure you should be aware of is the Crusher Crane. Try building one now from your Production Structures queue."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER40
	"*Crusher Cranes work much like Construction Yards, so now, you can build two structures at once from your two separate build queues."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER41
	"*What's more, your Crane's repair drones will automatically repair nearby vehicles, or you can order those vehicles into its grinders to crush them for a quick refund."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER42
	"*To access your newly-added build queues, click the buttons added to the Sidebar, or click the tabs in the Sidebar to cycle between queues."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER43
	"*To access your newly-added build queues, open the Command Menu with the Crusher Crane selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER44
	"*When you have multiple queues of a type available, you can cycle through them in the Command Menu by pressing the A button without moving the stick."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER45
	"*You can build multiple production structures to gain more build queues, allowing you to build more stuff at once. Of course, you'll need plenty of income to support this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER46
	"*Now, please feel free to continue exploring the richness of the Soviet build system."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER47
	"*When you're done, please select the Tsunami Tank to proceed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER48
	"*...I still think ours is better... Oh no."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER49
	"*Ow! OW!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER50
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI01
	"*Notice that the MCV's Unpack is a targeted special ability. Targeted abilities require you to select a target by placing your cursor over the terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI02
	"*Observe the ghosted image of the Construction Yard attached to your cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI03
	"*Now left-click anywhere on open terrain to open your MCV to unpack at that location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI04
	"*Now press the A button anywhere on open terrain to order your MCV to unpack at that location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI05
	"*Don't overdo it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI06
	"*Commander: Select the Power Plant button to begin building it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI07
	"*All Allied structures build over time inside the Construction Yard. Once they're ready, you'll be able to place them on the battlefield right away."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI08
	"*Your Power Plant is now ready to be placed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI09
	"*Simply left-click on its button and move your mouse over open terrain. Then left-click on an open spot on the terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI10
	"*Simply open the Command Menu and press the A button to select the Power Plant. Then press the A button on an open spot on the terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI11
	"*Bear in mind that a single Ore Refinery likely will not be enough to fund your military escapades."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI12
	"*Try to build an Ore Refinery next to each Ore Mine near your base, but be careful to defend them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI13
	"*Hai! Properly executed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI14
	"*Don't ask ridiculous questions!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI15
	"*Ore is the primary resource in Red Alert 3. Refineries automatically convert it to credits, which is the currency used to purchase all units and structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI16
	"*Ore Mines have a finite amount of resources that will eventually slow to trickle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI17
	"*So if you deplete an Ore Mine, it’s best to try and expand to another in order to maintain a steady income."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI18
	"*You can also halt the production of units or structures by right-clicking on a production button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI19
	"*Right-clicking a second time will cancel production and refund any credits that were spent. Left-clicking on a paused production process will resume production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI20
	"*You can also halt the production of units or structures by pressing the B button while you have them highlighted in the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI21
	"*Pressing B a second time will cancel production and refund any credits that were spent. Pressing button A on a paused production process will resume production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI22
	"*Observe, however, that Allied structures may only be built in the radius surrounding the Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI23
	"*You may expand your build radius by creating Command Hubs, which convert from your Prospectors."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI24
	"*Please select your Prospector and use its special ability to unpack it somewhere. Across the water, perhaps? Go ahead, commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI25
	"*Silence! Surely the Commander wants to move on to the other factions by now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI26
	"*Feel free to continue dabbling with the Allies, then select me when you are ready to continue."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI27
	"*This monstrosity is the Soviet Construction Yard. You will see that the Soviets build differently from the Allies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI28
	"*Select the Construction Yard or the Production Tab, then select the Reactor button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI29
	"*Select the Construction Yard and open the Command Menu, or just navigate to the Production Structures queue in the Command Menu. Then select the Reactor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI30
	"*Notice how the Command Menu closed automatically, to let you make your next move."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI31
	"*Now place the Reactor on open terrain, as you did with the Allied structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI32
	"*Do not wait for the Reactor to build in the queue, for you would wait... forever!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI33
	"*Unlike the Allies, the Soviets carelessly build their structures out on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI34
	"*At last. Let us continue, Commander, for this will be worth it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI35
	"*The Empire of the Rising Sun has the most unique build system in that our structures are all created from special units called Nano-Cores."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI36
	"*Cores may \"unfurl\" at the location of your choosing, much like an MCV unpacks into a Construction Yard. However: unfurled Imperial structures cannot pack back up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI37
	"*Go into your Production Structures queue and build a Generator Core."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI38
	"*The Generator Core will be yours to control as soon as it emerges from your Construction Yard. If you select it, you may give it move commands around the map like any unit."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI39
	"*To unfurl it into an Instant Generator, while having it selected, use its Unfurl special ability, much like you did with the MCV earlier in this lesson."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI40
	"*You should now have a ghosted image of the Instant Generator attached to your cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI41
	"*Select a spot on open terrain to make your Generator Core unfurl at that location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI42
	"*All Nano-Core are amphibious, so they can cross land as well as water. This means the Empire of the Rising Sun can spread its borders far and wide."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI43
	"*The Imperial Docks is the only structure that cannot unfurl on land, while the Mecha Bay and Instant Dojo cannot unfurl at sea."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI44
	"*One last thing about Imperial production structures: They must be upgraded individually to unlock new construction options. You'll find these upgrades in their build queues."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI45
	"*Now, Commander, do you see how superior our production capability is compared with that of my barbaric friends here?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN01
	"*Why hello again, Commander! In this lesson, you're gonna get acquainted with your units and some of the abilities that make them unique."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN02
	"*Every unit in Red Alert 3 has some sort of special ability, in addition to its primary ability. The majority of your units' primary abilities is to attack their targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN03
	"*A unit's special ability may put a nasty status effect on an enemy, switch to an alternate weapon, or even transform into an entirely different unit."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN04
	"*Oh, so that's how it is, then?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN05
	"*As stated earlier, not all special abilities need to be targeted like the Cryocopter's Shrink Beam. Some abilities cause units to switch weapon modes."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN06
	"*Blimey, that tank looks like he's lost control! And all you've got is an Allied Hydrofoil!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN07
	"*Its primary weapon is an anti-air cannon that won't do you any good here. However, if you use its special ability, it'll switch from its gun to the Weapon Jammer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN08
	"*Select the Hydrofoil now and ready the Weapon Jammer by left-clicking on its special ability button or hitting the F key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN09
	"*Select the Hydrofoil now and ready the Weapon Jammer by selecting it in the Command Menu, or pressing the X button while holding the Right Bumper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN10
	"*Proper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN11
	"*Now, have your Hydrofoil fire on that Soviet Apocalypse Tank on the shore."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN12
	"*Hah! So much for that tea party."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN13
	"*As you can see, the Apocalypse Tank can no longer fire. Not so scary now, is 'e?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN14
	"*So remember: Even the toughest enemy units may be vulnerable to your lesser units' special abilities. Learn them all, and never give up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN15
	"*No robots are gonna get past you, Commander!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN16
	"*You should know, there are some units at your disposal whose primary ability either isn't a weapon at all, or will change depending on what you tell it to attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN17
	"*For example, each faction has its own type of Engineer unit, like this swarthy fellow over here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN18
	"*Engineers are special units that can capture any enemy structure or neutral tech structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN19
	"*Much like with moving or attacking, you can select your Engineer and right-click on a capturable structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN20
	"*Much like with moving or attacking, you can select your Engineer, then press the A button on a capturable structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN21
	"*That'll make him go after it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN22
	"*Look, there seems to be an Oil Derrick you can capture out in the water. Oil Derricks are neutral tech structures that provide additional income."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN23
	"*Go get it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN24
	"*Off he goes! Note that Engineers are amphibious, so they automatically switch to a keen aquatic form when they get to water. Not all units are amphibious of course."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN25
	"*Notice you can issue capture commands into the fog of war. Assuming the structure is still there when you get to it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN26
	"*You may have noticed that when you highlighted that enemy structure with your Engineer selected, your cursor changed to a garrison cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN27
	"*That garrison cursor indicates a structure you can enter."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN28
	"*Your basic infantry can't garrison enemy structures or neutral tech structures like the Engineer can, but they can garrison civilian structures such as hotels and houses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN29
	"*When infantry garrison these structures, they receive extra protection as the building they're in will take damage instead of the units themselves, should they come under fire."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN30
	"*Garrisoning your units into civilian structures is both a good tactic both from an offensive and defensive perspective."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN31
	"*It helps to secure locations, force enemies to take an alternate path, or give your units more cover near to your base should the enemy send a force to destroy you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN32
	"*Now garrison that nearby structure by issuing a move order onto it whilst having some Peacekeepers selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN33
	"*Good, they're in. And here comes trouble."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN34
	"*As you can see, those enemy training robots fired upon the structure rather than directly at your Peacekeepers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN35
	"*Watch out, though, because each faction has ways of clearing out garrisoned structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN36
	"*Now, let's say you need to get your Peacekeepers out of the structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN37
	"*Just select the structure and use the Evacuate command, just like using a special ability on a unit."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN38
	"*Do this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN39
	"*Some of your units can also be garrisoned by your infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN40
	"*The Multigunner IFV is a unique Allied vehicle whose weapon takes on the characteristics of whichever infantry unit hops inside."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN41
	"*Order one of your Peacekeepers into that IFV and watch what happens."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN42
	"*Other units, such as our Allied Spies like this one here, also have contextual attacks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN43
	"*Select the Spy, then use his contextual attack on one of those enemy training dummies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN44
	"*Hahaha, now who's the dummy, am I right?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN45
	"*As you can see, the Spy's primary ability is to disguise himself as the enemy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN46
	"*Alternatively, if you highlight an enemy structure, you can try to infiltrate it to disrupt the enemy's base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN47
	"*C'mon, lads, we have to get through this. Commander, that's the end of this lesson. See you in the next one."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER01
	"*Wait, what...? No way, not me again!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER02
	"*Aaah, I'm melting!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER03
	"*Hey... Where did that Engineer go, anyway...?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER04
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER05
	"*Fear not, for civilians have long since abandoned such structures once they heard we were coming."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER06
	"*The Allies and Empire can try rushing their Peacekeepers or Imperial Warriors into a garrisoned structure, while the Soviet Conscripts can use their Molotov cocktails."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER07
	"*...If I may?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER08
	"*Normally the IFV's weapon works best against aircraft.  But once you garrisoned your Peacekeeper into it, it changed to an anti-infantry weapon."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER09
	"*While the IFV can only contain one infantry unit at a time, other vehicles can hold more, and can transport your infantry around the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER10
	"*For example, the Riptide ACV is admittedly a good transport for getting infantry quickly and safely from one point to another, although infantry cannot fire out of it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER11
	"*Garrison your remaining infantry into the Riptide now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER12
	"*Now that they're garrisoned, let's move your Riptide across this lake and over to the shore on the other side."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER13
	"*Look for the marker on the Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER14
	"*Riptides are a special type of unit in that they're amphibious, meaning they can traverse both land and water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER15
	"*As my comrade said, not all units are amphibious, so it's good to make note of the ones that are."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER16
	"*Some units behave differently on land and water. For instance, when your Riptide is on water, its torpedo tubes open to give it additional firepower."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER17
	"*Now that you've made it to the other side, let's get those Peacekeepers out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER18
	"*All transports have the not-so-special ability to evacuate their passengers. Use the Evacuate ability now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER19
	"*By the way, try pressing the directional pad in any direction to snap your cursor to the closest unselected target in that direction. This is useful for pinpointing targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER20
	"*Ooh…but why?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI01
	"*Let us go over how to use special abilities now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI02
	"*Select that Allied Cryocopter, if you please."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI03
	"*The Cryocopter's special ability is the Shrink Beam."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI04
	"*With the Cryocopter selected, left-click on its special ability button in the bottom right of your screen, or press the F key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI05
	"*Notice that the Shrink Beam is a targeted special ability, which means you have to left-click on a target to use it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI06
	"*With the Cryocopter selected, open the Command Menu and select its special ability, or hold the Right Bumper and press the X button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI07
	"*Notice that the Shrink Beam is a targeted special ability, which means you have to press the A button over a target to use it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI08
	"*Other types of special abilities take effect as soon as you press the ability button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI09
	"*Now then, use the Shrink Beam on my good friend the Soviet Hammer Tank."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI10
	"*Betrayed! After all we've been through!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI11
	"*If you're finished with your motivational speech, perhaps we can continue?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI12
	"*Commander, let's go over a unit whose special ability is... to transform!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI13
	"*One basic example is the MCV, though let us take a look at a more-exciting case in one of the Empire of the Rising Sun's versatile Mecha Tengu units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI14
	"*The Mecha Tengu is an amphibious hovering anti-infantry unit that can transform into the Jet Tengu, a flying air-superiority fighter."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI15
	"*Not only does the transform ability affect how it navigates the battlefield, it also means the unit changes from having anti-ground weapons to anti-air weapons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI16
	"*Select the Mecha Tengu and use its special ability."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI17
	"*Impressive, no? Now... order your Jet Tengu to destroy that miserable Cryocopter!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI18
	"*Oh, and don't worry -- it is merely a training robot carefully disguised to look like a real vehicle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI19
	"*He went into the structure, you fool! And there he shall remain, forever! For that is the Way of the Engineer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI20
	"*Of course, you could just blow the structures up if you cannot be bothered by such details."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI21
	"*Finally, let us discuss Contextual Attacks. A Contextual Attack is what you get when your cursor changes to something other than a normal attack cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI22
	"*Select the Allied commando who has showed up so very unexpectedly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI23
	"*This \"Agent Tanya\" has different ways of attacking targets, depending on the type of target."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI24
	"*When you order her to attack enemy infantry, such as these lifelike robots, your cursor will be that of a normal attack cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI25
	"*However, when you highlight an enemy vehicle or structure, you get a demolition cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI26
	"*When ordered to demolish a target, Tanya will move very close to the target, set some charges, and blow it up. This is an example of a contextual attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI27
	"*Go ahead and dispose of those forces using the commando."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI28
	"*Infiltration has different effects depending on which type of structure is infiltrated. Experiment with all the possibilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI29
	"*Incidentally, the Empire of the Rising Sun's Shinobi unit may also infiltrate structures. Only the tactless Soviets lack an infiltrator."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN01
	"*Why hello, hello, Commander!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN02
	"*In this particular lesson, we're going to be covering Top-Secret Protocols and how to use them, as well as the Threat Meter and some other heavy stuff."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN03
	"*To begin with, let's have a look at this here base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN04
	"*Let's say you're low on credits. If at any point you decide that you no longer want a structure that you’ve placed, you may sell it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN05
	"*To sell a structure, left-click on the Sell button under your Radar, then left-click on the structure you wish to sell. Right-clicking cancels out of Sell mode."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN06
	"*To sell a structure, bring up the Command Menu, select Sell Mode in the 11 o'clock position, then press the A button over a structure. Press B to cancel out of Sell mode."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN07
	"*Try selling one of those Power Plants now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN08
	"*Relax, friend, I was just about to explain to the Commander here how to repair. \nIt's pretty important."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN09
	"*To repair a damaged structure, left-click on the repair button under your radar. Then left click on your Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN10
	"*To repair a damaged structure, bring up the Command Menu, select Repair Mode in the 10 o'clock position, then press the A button over a damaged structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN11
	"*Give it a go."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN12
	"*Now then, let’s talk about Top-Secret Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN13
	"*Now let's go over how to access your Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN14
	"*Left-click the Top-Secret Protocols button, or press the Tilde hotkey to the left of the 1 key, to bring up a menu of all the dirty tricks you can use."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN15
	"*Open the Command Menu and drill down to your Support Powers in the 6 o'clock position. Then select the Top-Secret Protocols button in the center."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN16
	"*As you can see, this menu has, what, like 15 different Protocols to choose from."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN17
	"*The Protocols are ranked by levels, so to access Protocols further down the list, you need to access the ones above them first."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN18
	"*For example, you can't get Cryoshot until you get Surveillance Sweep."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN19
	"*Each Protocol costs one Security Point."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN20
	"*Now, go get Surveillance Sweep from your Top-Secret Protocols menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN21
	"*Well well, sir, looks like you've been cleared to use Surveillance Sweep! What an occasion!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN22
	"*All protocols available to you will appear on the left-hand side of your screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN23
	"*To use Surveillance Sweep, first left-click on it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN24
	"*To use Surveillance Sweep, open the Command Menu, drill down to your Support Powers, and select it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN25
	"*Now you need to select a target location for the sweep."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN26
	"*This one's a little dodgy because you then have to select a second location to plot a trajectory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN27
	"*So left-click once, then again someplace else in the area near the edge of the screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN28
	"*So, press button A in one area, then again someplace else near the edge of the screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN29
	"*Give it a go."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN30
	"*See that? Make sure to have a look at the notes written next to each Protocol so you're aware of what you're signing up for before you pick one of these."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN31
	"*By the way, the Protocols available to you are determined solely by the faction you're commanding."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN32
	"*So even if you pull a stunt like capturing an enemy ConYard, doesn't mean their top brass will open the kimono on their military secrets. Makes sense, yeah?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN33
	"*Watch how one of your units gains veterancy by mowing down droves of hostile targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN34
	"*Heroic forces like these can make a huge difference, so best keep 'em around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN35
	"*Speaking of which...what's all the commotion over there?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN36
	"*Oh-hohoho, now it's on!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN37
	"*Try to build up enough forces to stop your enemy's invasion, then take those units to the enemy's base and destroy it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN38
	"*Take note as you build units that your Command Point total keeps increasing. This represents the total sum of units you can have in the field at one time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN39
	"*Smashing work, commander. You're now one step closer to becoming a serious threat out there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN40
	"*We're done with this lesson. See you in the next one, all right."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER01
	"*He was a good Power Plant... but you can build another."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER02
	"*Don't go crazy selling everything. What would your friends think if you failed a tutorial mission?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER03
	"*Hey--! Quit it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER04
	"*You'll notice that a repair icon has appeared on your Construction Yard, indicating that it's undergoing repairs."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER05
	"*Structures can only repair as long as you have sufficient funds. You may notice that as your structure is repairing, your credits are slowly trickling down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER06
	"*Top-Secret Protocols is just a fancy term for special support powers you can use. These will affect the battlefield, your enemies, and your units and structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER07
	"*Basically, they can get you out of a pinch."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER08
	"*Keep in mind, you need your Construction Yard intact in order to use them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER09
	"*As mentioned earlier, there are different types of Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER10
	"*There are offense-oriented protocols such as Surgical Strike, which can damage enemy forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER11
	"*There are more-tactical protocols such as Chrono Rift, which can protect your units or split enemy forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER12
	"*And then there are upgrade protocols that provide passive bonuses, such as Advanced Aeronautics, which toughens up all those weak little Allied aircraft."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER13
	"*Unlike offensive and tactical protocols, upgrade protocols take effect immediately once acquired and do not need to be activated manually."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER14
	"*Next we'll talk about the Threat Meter, which gives you an impression of how much death and destruction is happening all around you in a given moment."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER15
	"*The Threat Meter increases in battle, especially when you sustain heavy casualties, and the higher it is, the faster you earn new Security Points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER16
	"*Higher levels of threat also influence how quickly your units gain combat veterancy. The higher the threat, the faster your units will become great heroes from killing foes!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER17
	"*Veteran units display a little chevron. They're better at killing enemies, and once they achieve Heroic status, they automatically regenerate to boot."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER18
	"*Remember, you also have access to your Top Secret Protocols to help you take down your enemy!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER19
	"*Ow!! Whatever, figure out yourself then!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI01
	"*Each faction has its own set of Protocols, which can be offensive or defensive in nature--sometimes both."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI02
	"*As you progress through a battle, you'll gradually earn Security Points, which you can use to access new Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI03
	"*Progress towards your next Security Point is indicated by the meter surrounding the Top-Secret Protocols button on your screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI04
	"*The number in the button is your current number of Security Points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI05
	"*Progress towards your next Security Point is indicated by a special meter next to your Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI06
	"*The number beside the meter is your current number of Security Points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI07
	"*It appears you are under attack. Take advantage of your high threat meter and vet up your forces while using some of your Top-Secret Protocols to assist you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI08
	"*Fear not, for this is only a simulation involving lifelike robots."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN01
	"*Back for more, then, Commander? In this particular lesson, we’ll be going over some of the more-advanced play mechanics that'll separate the men from the boys."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN02
	"*From earlier lessons, you should be aware of the Allied Spy and some of his capabilities by now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN03
	"*Spies can disguise themselves as enemy units. Only scout units--the Allied Attack Dog, Soviet War Bear, and Imperial Burst Drone--can detect disguised enemy units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN04
	"*Spies and Imperial Shinobi can also infiltrate enemy structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN05
	"*When you infiltrate a structure, it'll impair your enemy's base in various ways, which should give you the upper hand."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN06
	"*For example, if you infiltrate their enemy Reactor, the entire base will power down for a while."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN07
	"*Go ahead and infiltrate the Instant Generator by right clicking on in it whilst your Spy is selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN08
	"*Go ahead and infiltrate the Instant Generator by moving your cursor over it and pressing button A whilst your Spy is selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN09
	"*Good job, sir. Your units made it back and were able to whittle down those enemy tanks' health enough for your base defenses to finish them off."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN10
	"*Had you issued a normal move order back to your base, your Guardian Tanks might not have fared as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN11
	"*Incidentally, should the enemy catch you off guard with an attack, listen for audio cues from your Intel Officer and visual cues on Radar to tip you off."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN12
	"*To jump to the most recent Radar event, just hit the Space Bar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN13
	"*Or to get back to your main base from anywhere in battle, tap the H key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN14
	"*To jump to the most recent Radar event, just hit the BACK button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN15
	"*Or to get back to your main base, click the Left Stick button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN16
	"*Ah, pants. It looks like the Empire is sending another attack wave, but this time they've come at us with infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN17
	"*Your base defenses are strong against infantry, but with that many of the blighters, I don't think it's going to be enough."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN18
	"*So, a good way to dispatch large quantities of infantry is to crush them with vehicles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN19
	"*Not all vehicles can crush infantry so it's good to familiarize yourself with the ones that can."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN20
	"*Small vehicles like your IFVs and Riptides are examples of vehicles that can't crush."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN21
	"*On the other hand, larger vehicles like Guardian Tanks and Assault Destroyers can crush a man like so many potato crisps!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN22
	"*What's more, some of the largest vehicles in Red Alert 3 are big enough to crush other, smaller vehicles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN23
	"*Anyhow - let's crush those robots!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN24
	"*Thought you'd never ask! To crush enemy infantry, select your Guardian Tanks and issue a move order behind the enemy infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN25
	"*You can also issue a Force-Move command using the G hotkey or using the Advanced Commands tab near the bottom of the screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN26
	"*You can also issue a Force-Move command by pressing the A button on your target while holding the Right Bumper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN27
	"*Issue a move command to the designated location with your tanks now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN28
	"*Seeing as how that Rising Sun base seems intent on taking us down, let's go over some ways to get your units to protect your base without being drawn out by the enemy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN29
	"*All of your units can be set to different stances, which affect their behavior."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN30
	"*All units start off in Guard Stance, meaning they will auto-acquire enemies that come within their attack range, and pursue them for a short distance if they try to flee."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN31
	"*Once the dust settles, your units will return to their original positions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN32
	"*We need to have some of our units on defense for our base but not pursue our enemies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN33
	"*To do this, we need to put them into Hold Ground Stance. First, select one or more of your tanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN34
	"*Now click on the Advanced Commands panel in the bottom right of your screen next to the unit portrait."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN35
	"*As you can see, this panel reveals some additional controls for your units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN36
	"*Now open the Command Menu and take a look at all the available stance options."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN37
	"*Select the Hold Ground button to change your units' stance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN38
	"*Perfect. What say we also set up some base defenses? Each faction has a couple of its own base defenses. The Allies have Multigunner Turrets, for example."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN39
	"*Select the Support Structures tab in the Sidebar, build a Multigunner Turret, and place it near your tanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN40
	"*Open the Command Menu, navigate to your Support Structures queue, and build a Multigunner Turret. Then place it near your tanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN41
	"*Multigunner Turrets change weapons if you put different infantry into them, though the rocket launchers they use by default should be handy in most cases."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN42
	"*I've been meaning to tell you, by the way: If you have units selected and you open the Command Menu, you can back up to the top level just by pushing the B button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN43
	"*You don't need to deselect anybody."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN44
	"*Then, if you want to get back to your selected units, drill down to the Current Selection button located in the 7 o'clock position in the Command Menu,"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN45
	"*Capital. Now if the Rising Sun attacks, we'll have some extra defenses waiting for them that they won't be able to draw away from out base. And here they come!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN46
	"*As you can see, they've decided to retreat back to base, but your Guardian Tanks stood their ground and didn't continue after them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN47
	"*Had your Guardian Tanks followed them back, they most likely would have been destroyed by the Empire's own base defenses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN48
	"*Well, good job, Commander. You now know some of the advanced tactics that'll surely make you a worthy adversary on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN49
	"*And would you believe it? There are still more advanced tactics and commands for you to learn. Just dig into the options screen for a complete command list."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN50
	"*But do that on your own time. This lesson's over, and there's only one more left. We're heading over to it now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER01
	"*Excellent, Commander! By infiltrating their Generator, you've brought down their entire base's power, which in turn powered down their base defenses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER02
	"*That will certainly make it easier to destroy their base! Stupid robots!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER03
	"*Oh no! It appears the Empire of the Rising Sun is sending in a force to destroy your tanks. You'll need to retreat your tanks back to your base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER04
	"*A clever way of doing that is to Reverse-Move them back to your base. This will allow them to continue attacking those enemy units while retreating to a safer location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER05
	"*To Reverse-Move your units, select them and press the D key on your keyboard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER06
	"*Notice how your cursor changed. Right-click on the target destination near your Construction Yard to order your tanks to retreat."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER07
	"*To Reverse-Move your units, select them, hold down the Right Bumper, and press the A button. Go ahead and have your tanks retreat to your Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER07A
	"*To Reverse-Move your units, select them, hold down the Right Bumper, and press the A button. Go ahead and have your tanks retreat to your Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER08
	"*Another benefit of Reverse-Moving is that it keeps a unit's stronger front armor facing the enemy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER09
	"*Most vehicles are more vulnerable from the rear and flanks, so when you retreat from enemies using a normal move command, you'll turn tail and take more damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER10
	"*Reverse-moving allows you units' stronger front armor to take the brunt of the fire."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER11
	"*Ew...."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER12
	"*Simple as that, you've just changed your units' stance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER13
	"*Keep in mind that no matter what stance your units are in, any orders you issue will always be followed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER14
	"*Stances will only affect how units behave when not under your direct control."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER15
	"*Now, take three Guardian Tanks, not counting our field-instructor, and move one to each of the designated locations and put them into Hold Ground stance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER16
	"*You can also build walls from your Support Structures queue. To do so, build and place one wall segment, then build and place another along the same row as the first."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER17
	"*You'll see the build grid show green to indicate where you can form a solid wall. Careful, though. Each wall segment costs you, so longer walls are more expensive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER18
	"*Walls are useful for blocking smaller forces, like those pesky Engineers always trying to steal your structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER19
	"*Go on and try building a solid wall at the front of your base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER20
	"*Ow! What was that for?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK01
	"*Wait."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK02
	"*You may wish to assign your tanks to a Control Group first. This is an important way of managing your forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK03
	"*To assign units to a Control Group, select them, then hold the Control key and press a number key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK04
	"*To assign units to a Control Group, select them, and hold the X button while holding the Left Bumper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK05
	"*Do this now, please."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK06
	"*Good."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK07
	"*You may now select those units at any time by pressing the corresponding number key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK08
	"*You can also jump to the group by double-tapping the key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK09
	"*You may now select those units at any time just by tapping the X button while holding the Left Bumper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK10
	"*You can also jump to the group, or anything you have selected, by pressing the Y button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK11
	"*One further note about control groups: All units are placed into Control Groups automatically."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK12
	"*To access these, open the Command Menu, and select Control Groups in the 8 o'clock position. There you will always be able to select any of your units by type."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK13
	"*Now... please proceed with crushing my robots."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK14
	"*Yes, the Empire's base defenses are quite impressive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK15
	"*You may need to use combined arms to defeat them. In fact, if you depend overmuch on just one or two types of units, you are bound to fail."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK16
	"*Thankfully, it is easy to manage multiple types of units at once."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK17
	"*Try selecting all your combat forces on the battlefield using the Q key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK18
	"*One tap of Q selects all units onscreen. Two taps selects all units on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK19
	"*Good. Notice you have multiple unit types in the contextual tab in your Sidebar at right."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK20
	"*One type of unit in your group will always be selected. To cycle between unit types, simply tap the Tab hotkey. Try this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK21
	"*Yes, that's it. You may also cycle unit types in reverse order by pressing the Tab key while holding the Shift key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK22
	"*Try selecting all your combat forces on the battlefield by double-tapping the X button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK23
	"*Good. Notice that when you open the Command Menu, you have multiple unit types selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK24
	"*If you wish to reduce your selection to just one unit type, highlight it in the Command Menu and press and hold the A button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK25
	"*If you wish to reduce your selection to just one unit type, highlight it in the Command Menu and tap the A button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK26
	"*You may navigate to different unit types in the Command Menu to use their special abilities or change their stances."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK27
	"*Or, without opening the Command Menu, simply hold the Right Bumper while tapping up or down on the D-pad to cycle between unit types."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK28
	"*Switching unit types in this fashion makes it easier to use your mixed group's special abilities, without deselecting the group."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK29
	"*We should also briefly touch on Waypoint Mode, for it's useful. Waypoint Mode lets you queue up move or attack orders."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK30
	"*To use Waypoint Mode, hold the Alt key while issuing move or attack orders as normal with units selected. Your units will complete the orders in sequence."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK31
	"*To use Waypoint Mode, hold the Left Bumper while issuing move or attack orders as normal with units selected. Your units will complete the orders in sequence."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK32
	"*Now, earlier we had mentioned how directional armor comes into play during battles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK33
	"*Another type of armor bonus your units can receive comes from an automatic reaction to enemy fire called suppression."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK34
	"*Suppression only affects infantry units. When infantry units become suppressed, they go prone on the ground and continue firing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK35
	"*Suppressed infantry are slower but more resistant to damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK36
	"*Send your infantry into that city square there and attack that garrisoned structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK37
	"*Banzi! As you approached the structure, your units came under enemy fire and some of them were suppressed as a result of the enemy attacks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK38
	"*Due to this suppressed position, your units could absorb more damage and in turn deal more damage to that enemy structure, allowing them to destroy it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK39
	"*That... was for my robots...!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_COOLEG01
	"*My work here is done, my friend. I'll see you on the other side, where the real action is!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN01
	"*Finally, the last lesson! Feels good to be almost finished, eh Commander? Let's get started."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN02
	"*In this lesson, you'll learn how to work with your Co-Commander to help achieve victory on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN03
	"*You'll be working with a Co-Commander throughout the campaigns in Red Alert 3."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN04
	"*You can fight alongside a friend, or if you don't have any friends, the game will provide one for you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN05
	"*No matter which campaign you're playing, your Co-Commander's forces will always be green."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN06
	"*No matter which campaign you're playing, your Co-Commander's forces will always be gold."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN07
	"*In general, you can expect your Co-Commander to do a halfway-decent job of fending for him- or herself or helping you out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN08
	"*But just in case, we've set up a handy-dandy interface for you to issue specific directives to your partner."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN09
	"*In the upper left hand of your screen is the Co-Commander Monitor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN10
	"*Unfortunately this won't let you control your real friends, but it's useful when fighting alongside one of the game's Co-Commanders."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN11
	"*Now, the next directive is Strike Target. This directive makes your Co-Commander immediately send available forces to destroy that target, and anything nearby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN12
	"*Much like last time, to issue a Strike Target directive you must first select the button. Then move your cursor over an enemy and left click on it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN13
	"*Much like last time, to issue a Strike Target directive you must hold the Left Bumper, then tap right on the D-pad. Then select a target with button A."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN14
	"*Issue a Strike Target directive on that enemy Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN15
	"*See that? Your Co-Commander's always got your back, Commander!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN16
	"*Lastly, let's go over the Keep Command directive. This one makes your Co-Commander fend for him- or herself, and he or she will always do so by default."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN17
	"*Unlike the other directives, this one does not require you to select a target, and may be used to cancel the other directives."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN18
	"*To issue this directive, simply select the Keep Command button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN19
	"*To issue the Keep Command directive, hold the Left Bumper and tap down on the D-Pad."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN20
	"*Try this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN21
	"*To give your Co-Commander the signal to execute the Strike, select it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN22
	"*To give your Co-Commander the signal to execute the Strike, select it and open the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN23
	"*This brings up a window explaining the strike. To confirm the tactic, select the Execute button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN24
	"*Go ahead and give your Co-Commander the signal now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN25
	"*You may also choose to cancel a Co-Commander Strike that's already in progress."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN26
	"*On that note, great job, Commander.  You now have the know-how to work with your Co-Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN27
	"*As you can see, your Co-Commander can help you do some of the heavy lifting."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN28
	"*Now get out there, and knock some heads together!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN29
	"*Go on, what are you waiting for, a fancy ending with a sappy montage?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN30
	"*As for you, boys...? The truce is off!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER01
	"*Now let's go over all the functions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER02
	"*First and foremost, there's a handsome image of your Co-Commander to remind you who you're fighting alongside."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER03
	"*For this tutorial you'll be fighting alongside the fresh-faced Soviet Commander Oleg."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER04
	"*Right next to his portrait are the various directives you can issue. Basically, you can boss him around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER05
	"*The first is Take Position, which causes your Co-Commander to immediately send his available forces to a target location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER06
	"*To issue this directive, select the Take Position button. Then move your cursor over the battlefield and left-click again in a target area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER07
	"*To issue this directive, hold the Left Bumper and tap Left on the D-Pad. Then move your cursor over the battlefield and press the A button in the target area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER08
	"*Go ahead, please."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER09
	"*Good. Notice how Oleg promptly responded by sending his forces to the position you requested."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER10
	"*Alternatively, you may open the Command Menu and drill down to the Communicator, located in the 9 o'clock position. Here you will find the different directives available."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER11
	"*That is how we do it in Russia! Notice how Oleg immediately responded with his forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER12
	"*Another option is to use the Plan Attack directive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER13
	"*This directive makes your Co-Commander build a good-sized force to eliminate any enemy units in the target area, as well as any enemies encountered along the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER14
	"*As with the others, to issue a Plan Attack directive, just select the button, then select a target enemy or location on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER15
	"*As with the others, to issue a Plan Attack directive, hold down the Left Bumper and tap Up on the D-pad. Then select a target area using button A."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER16
	"*Go ahead and use Plan Attack on the other side of that valley."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER17
	"*Finally!! You jerks!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI01
	"*Now then. We have one final type of directive to review."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI02
	"*During the course of some missions, you will come across what we call Co-Commander Strikes. These are situational tactics your co-commander will use when given the signal."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI03
	"*Notice how one has just appeared on the battlefield. Co-Commander Strikes may appear anywhere, anytime during a mission, and it's yours to decide how best to use them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI04
	"*Let us examine that Co-Commander Strike more closely."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI05
	"*Shut up!!"
End

DiskCostDlg_Title
	"[ProductName] Setup"
End

DiskCostDlgDescription
	"The disk space required for the installation of the game."
End

DiskCostDlgText_Hide
	"Highlighted volumes do not have enough disk space available. You can either remove some files from the highlighted volumes, or select different destination drives."
End

DiskCostDlgTitle
	"{\\WixUI_Font_Title}Disk Space Requirements"
End

DiskPromptString_1
	"Command and Conquer(tm) Red Alert(tm) 3"
End

EasyInfoShortcutName
	"EAsy Info"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN01DESC
	"Thanks for playing the Red Alert 3 beta! Please play as much as you like, and share your experiences, tips, and strategies at www.redalert3.com."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN02DESC
	"Units in Red Alert 3 each have a unique special ability. How effectively you use these will decide the outcome of your battles! To quickly use the selected unit's ability, just hit the \"F\" hotkey."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN03DESC
	"Scouting is essential to victory. Try quickly training up a scout unit and take it to the enemy's base to see what he's got in store for you. Then create the appropriate counters, and have at it!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN04DESC
	"Remember to purchase and use your Top-Secret Protocols, which are special powers that can get you out of a pinch or turn the tide of battle. To get new powers, click the button in the lower-left corner of the screen!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN05DESC
	"Get more income by expanding to as many Ore Mines as you can! In general, you should place an Ore Refinery in the spot right in front of an Ore Mine, and you only need one Ore Collector per Mine."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN06DESC
	"Capture those Neutral Tech Structures! An Oil Derrick boosts your cash flow, Observation Posts reveal the surrounding fog of war, and more! These structures can swing the battle in your favor."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN07DESC
	"Go navy! An amphibious or pure-naval strategy can catch your opponent by surprise, while giving you free reign over vast portions of the battlefield."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN08DESC
	"Terror Drones got you in a tizzy? Simply drive your infected vehicles back to one of your vehicle production structures (or the Soviet Crusher Crane) and their repair drones will fix you right up!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN09DESC
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun upgrades its production structures individually, by researching Nanotech Upgrade and Nanotech Breakthrough, respectively. These unlock new construction options in a structure."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN10DESC
	"Defend your Ore Collectors at all costs! They may crush enemy infantry as a last resort, and some have unique defensive abilities. If you do lose a Collector, you can build another from your Refinery."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN11DESC
	"We're not finished yet! Please note that everything you experience in this beta is work-in-progress. Your feedback will influence how the game finally takes shape, so tell us what you think!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN12DESC
	"Thanks for playing the Red Alert 3 beta! The full version of the game will feature three fully cooperative campaigns, intense skirmish battles against ruthless enemy commanders, and more!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN13DESC
	"Beware of Spies! The Allies' Spy unit may disguise himself as any other infantry. Sniff him out with your faction's scout unit, before he gets close enough to cause any trouble!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN14DESC
	"The Soviet Hammer Tank features the devious Leech-Beam special ability, which can siphon enemy armor and even weapons! Once you've stolen a weapon, switch back to primary firing mode for twice the punch!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN15DESC
	"The Allied Spy and the Imperial Shinobi may infiltrate enemy structures, causing all sorts of bad things to happen to their foes. The consequences of infiltration depend on which type of structure is infiltrated."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN16DESC
	"CRYOCOPTER - The Allies' incredible Cryocopter may freeze enemy surface units, rendering them immobile and extremely vulnerable to attack! Cryocopters may also shrink units down to embarrasing, crushable proportions!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN17DESC
	"CENTURY BOMBER - The Allies' sturdy heavy bomber can pound enemy structures into dust in a carpet-bombing run, then paradrop infantry units behind enemy lines so they can finish off anything left standing."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN18DESC
	"VINDICATOR - The Allies' close-support sortie bomber is perfect for swooping in to put a serious dent into enemy armor divisions. Should it come under anti-aircraft fire, it can autopilot back to base in a snap."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN19DESC
	"MIRAGE TANK - The Allies' high-tech Mirage Tank is the ultimate anti-tank assassin. Its spectrum cannon can tear through armor, and it camouflages itself while still. Plus its special ability makes nearby units invisible!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN20DESC
	"APOCALYPSE TANK - The heaviest tank ever made. As if this monstrosity's twin cannons were not enough, its magnetic harpoon can prevent faster foes from escaping its destructive attacks."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN21DESC
	"TSUNAMI TANK - The mainline Imperial tank is uniquely capable of traversing both land and sea. Its fast-firing main gun can punch through any armor soon enough, and its special ability infuses the vehicle with a significant defensive boost."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN22DESC
	"SEA-WING - The Sea-Wing is a submersible unit that can take down enemy aircraft in a flurry of missiles. The latest model can convert to the flying Sky-Wing form, which is effective at assaulting enemy infantry from above."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN23DESC
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun's anti-air options revolve around its transforming forces! Try switching to the secondary modes of your Defender-VX base defense or Mecha Tengu to take down those aircraft!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN24DESC
	"The Allies must advance their tech at each of their expansion bases independently. Research Heightened Clearance to unlock the second tier of units, then get up to Max Clearance for the mightiest forces of all!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN25DESC
	"Submersible units such as the Soviets' Akula Sub are invulnerable to most attacks and invisible to enemy Radar while under water! However, they must surface in order to attack their targets."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN26DESC
	"Remember Reverse-Move! You can make certain units move in reverse by using the \"D\" hotkey. This lets you continue firing on an enemy target while drawing him into your carefully-laid traps!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN27DESC
	"Have you tried building your base exclusively on water? If you're up against an opponent who relies too heavily on ground forces, get out to sea and mount an amphibious assault!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN28DESC
	"Make sure your base is fully powered at all times! Keeping your power levels in the green keeps your base defenses online and your production structures cranking away at full speed!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN29DESC
	"The Soviet Super-Reactor can solve all your power needs! Just don't let your enemies blow it up or it's liable to destroy half your base. Try selling this structure before it explodes!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN30DESC
	"The frontline infantry unit on each faction can counter enemy units garrisoned in buildings! Peacekeepers and Imperial Warriors just need to get inside, while Conscripts can toss their Molotov cocktails."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN31DESC
	"BURST DRONE - Imperial Burst Drones can latch onto and slow down your vehicles and aircraft, and even self-destruct to deal damage! Shoot them down using anti-air units, or by targeting any vehicles they've attached themselves to."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN32DESC
	"If the enemy is attempting to capture your Construction Yard with an Engineer, you can always pack up into an MCV to thwart his sneaky strategy! Then crush the Engineer and experience sweet revenge!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN33DESC
	"TESLA TROOPER - Not even a tank can crush the Soviet Tesla Trooper, who can obliterate most targets with his electrifying attack. His special ability is to switch on an EM disruption field, which disables enemy vehicles nearby."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN34DESC
	"TESLA TANK - Available in limited supply only to the highest-ranking officials, Tesla Tanks are experimental new forces combining the durability and mobility of a fast-assault vehicle with the raw power of Tesla weaponry."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREENTITLE
	"Command & Conquer Red Alert 3 Beta"
End

ECS:ENGAGINGCONTENTDESC
	"The battle is about to commence. Battlefield control interface coming online. Construction Yard uplink imminent. Good luck, commander."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDACKERMANDESC
	"PRESIDENT HOWARD T. ACKERMAN - This staunch anti-communist and pro-capitalist ideologue won the American election by a landslide. He's very supportive of the Allied coalition effort, at least when it comes to fighting back against the Soviet Union. Born and raised on a farm in Idaho, Ackerman energized his nation with grass-roots, roll-up-his-sleeves style."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDAPOLLODESC
	"APOLLO FIGHTER - The Allies' Apollo Fighter is one of the fastest, most reliable air superiority fighters in the world. Its twin autocannons can shred enemy aircraft, and it can quickly return to base if threatened by anti-aircraft fire."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDASSAULTDESTROYERDESC
	"ASSAULT DESTROYER - The Allies' state-of-the-art amphibious warship features a powerful swivel-mounted main gun as well as the unique Black Hole Armor, which draws enemy firepower in the vicinity. Now that's taking one for the team!"
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDBINGHAMDESC
	"FIELD MARSHALL ROBERT BINGHAM - The chief of the Allies' military forces earned his position through decades of selflessly protecting the freedoms of the Allied nations. A wise and rational military and political leader, Bingham is known to have a keen eye for good tactics and talent, and rarely seems affected by the heavy burden of his post."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDCHRONOSPHERE2DESC
	"In recent years, the Allies have managed to withstand the Soviet onslaught using various unorthodox new weapons and technologies, such as the Chronosphere. Much of this equipment was jointly developed by the Allied Nations, in partnership with advanced defense research firms such as FutureTech."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDCHRONOSPHEREDESC
	"The Allies recently unlocked the secrets of matter-transport technology in the Chronosphere, one of many cutting-edge engineering marvels developed in secret by the minds at FutureTech. The Chronosphere offers nearly limitless tactical possibilities to the shrewd battlefield commander."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDEVADESC
	"LIEUTENANT EVA McKENNA - Eva was the best student in her academy classes year after year, and now personally attends to the highest-ranking members of Allied coalition, ensuring a strong chain of command. Affected by the Soviet-Allied conflict from a young age, she has dedicated her life to serving the Allied cause."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDPROTOAPOLLODESC
	"Because the Allied Nations are linked by a common enemy and ideology rather than by national borders, it is little wonder that they possess one of the finest air forces in the world. Necessity forced the Allies to rapidly prototype their aircraft designs into today's highly-efficient models."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDTANYA2DESC
	"SPECIAL AGENT TANYA - Some say Tanya is invincible, though the Soviets have sought to disprove this theory. They learned, however, that their conscripts were no match for her exceptional marksmanship, and even their mightiest battle tanks were vulnerable to her skill with explosive charges."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDTANYA3DESC
	"TANYA'S TIME BELT - Though Tanya travels light, she is never without her trusty Time Belt, a unique prototype developed by the sharp minds at FutureTech. This device is able to put a slight crease in the fabric of time by whisking Tanya back to her position several seconds ago."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDTANYADESC
	"SPECIAL AGENT TANYA - This incredibly skilled American operative is often asked to undertake the Allies' most dangerous missions. When she isn't in combat, chances are she is gathering critical mission intel by any means necessary. She has written authority to speak freely at all times."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP01
	"All commanders are advised to keep their bases fully powered at all times. Without enough power structures, your units and structures will build more slowly and your base defenses will cease functioning."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP02
	"Use combined arms to achieve victory! A well-balanced combat group includes an assortment of anti-infantry, anti-vehicle, and anti-aircraft forces. Avoid relying too heavily on any one type of unit to prevent your enemies from easily countering your armies."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP03
	"If your Construction Yard comes under heavy fire from enemy vehicles, it is advisable to escape to the waters (or onto land, as the case may be). Mobile Construction Vehicles are amphibious, and although they have no weapons, they are large enough to crush most enemies under their treads."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP04
	"Bombardment vehicles excel at taking down enemy base defenses. Should your enemy hunker down using advanced base defenses, roll in artillery to destroy them from long range! Better yet, take out the enemy's power structures to cause all those base defenses to shut down."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP05
	"Fortress Walls, available in the Support Structures queue, can be used to slow enemy troop movements and prevent enemy Engineers, Infiltrators, and Commandos from getting into your structures."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP06
	"If an enemy unit seems invincible, chances are there's a better way to fight it. Even the biggest, toughest combat vehicle has its weaknesses, and large groups of foes are all the more vulnerable to area-of-effect attacks. Mix up your tactics and keep the enemy guessing!"
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP07
	"Your forces will not automatically attack enemy structures by default, in case you want to capture or infiltrate those structures. If you plan on laying waste to the enemy's base, try switching your forces to Aggressive Stance, or use the Assault-Move command."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP08
	"Seasoned commanders agree: In battle, it's best to keep spending one's credits without exceeding one's income. This way you'll be building new military forces and additional structures at a good clip. Don't get caught sitting on thousands of credits with no army to defend them! "
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP09
	"If a strategy is ineffective, immediately discontinue its use! Avoid relying too heavily on any one tactic, lest your opponents catch on and bring the right counters. Keeping your enemies guessing is the key to victory."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGILESDESC
	"COMMANDER GILES PRICE - This one-time fighter ace happily accepted a desk job since it put so many more shiny chevrons on his lapel. Now he's quickly making a name for himself as a capable, cool-headed tactician. He oversees one of the Allies' finest strategic air bases in Europe."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANEXPANSIONDESC
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun may expand to unclaimed Ore Mines quickly using its Refinery Cores. Imperial Ore Collectors even possess a special defensive weapon for use against enemies that dare threaten resourcing operations."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANMECHAKINGDESC
	"SHOGUN EXECUTIONER - Unrivaled, Prince Tatsu's near-unstoppable creation has cut a path through the Soviet countryside. Now its six eyes are set squarely on the Union's capital city. Its mission has been hard-coded: Moscow and the Kremlin must be utterly destroyed, the Soviets' time-machine along with them."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANNAVYDESC
	"The Imperial navy is as versatile as it is deadly, often taking the Empire's enemies by surprise using amphibious assaults or long-range bombardment. Consider the seas unsafe when the Rising Sun's afoot. "
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANSHINOBIDESC
	"SHINOBI - These hooded assassin-saboteurs are responsible for gathering intelligence for the Empire of the Rising Sun, as well as for putting its most-hated enemies to the sword. While the Imperial Shinobi are armed only with archaic, old-fashioned weapons, they have proven to be uncommonly lethal."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANSHOGUNDESC
	"SHOGUN BATTLESHIP - The largest, most powerful members of the Empire of the Rising Sun's naval armadas are armed with six main gun batteries that can shatter even the most heavily-fortified enemy compounds from great range. To helm such a vessel is one of the Empire's highest honors."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANSUKIDESC
	"LOGISTICAL OFFICER SUKI TOYAMA - One of the most trusted officers of the Empire of the Rising Sun, Suki is a childhood friend of Prince Tatsu and was born to serve an important post within the Imperial military hierarchy. She is responsible for relaying military intelligence to Imperial commanders, and is authorized to speak directly to the Emperor himself."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANTATSUDESC
	"CROWN PRINCE TATSU - The Emperor Yoshiro's only son, and the visionary behind the Empire of the Rising Sun's unprecedented military technology. Less traditional than his father yet just as driven, Prince Tatsu is widely considered a brilliant and pragmatic leader seeking to modernize and strengthen the Empire."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANYOSHIRODESC
	"EMPEROR YOSHIRO - The longtime ruler of the Empire of the Rising Sun, cherished as a living god by his people. Emperor Yoshiro is a traditionalist who strictly follows the code of bushido, the samurai way of the warrior. He fundamentally believes that the Rising Sun’s destiny is to rule the entire world."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENKENJIDESC
	"COMMANDER KENJI TENZAI - This extremely confident officer is famous for his way with sophisticated technology and, at least in his mind, many other reasons. Kenji was put in charge of field-testing the Empire's newest fighting forces by Prince Tatsu himself, and likely has his affluent family to thank for it."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENLISSETTEDESC
	"COMMANDER LISSETTE HANLEY - As a former spy serving the Allied Special Forces, Lissette has deep insight into enemy strategies, as well as a one-of-a-kind knowledge of the Allies' most-sophisticated weapons. Her casual, almost-playful manner hints at years of experience in tense combat situations."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENMOSKVINDESC
	"COMMANDER NIKOLAI MOSKVIN - This intense young man quickly rose through the ranks of the Red Army's largest Tesla Trooper regiment due to his unconventional yet brutally effective tactics, and now oversees the Union's experimental forces. Some say he is psychologically unstable... but never to his face."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENNAOMIDESC
	"COMMANDER NAOMI SHIRADA - This gifted, no-nonsense fleet commander is heiress to a famous military family's legacy and is widely known to have little patience for those who get in her way of her ambitions. It is said she has no permanent home, preferring life aboard the ships in the armadas at her disposal."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENOLEGDESC
	"COMMANDER OLEG VODNIK - Although casualty rates among Soviet conscripts are very high, opportunities for advancement abound for those who survive the front lines. Oleg is living proof of this. In spite of his informal demeanor, he has a proven ability to lead in battle and is well-liked by most of his men."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSHINZODESC
	"COMMANDER SHINZO NAGAMA - A calculating military leader who comes from a long line of Imperial military advisors seeking the Empire's rise to absolute power. Shinzo was one of the architects of the Imperial invasion of the Soviet Union, and has taken it upon himself to train a new generation of commanders."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETAIRFIELDDESC
	"The Soviet airforce has grown bold in recent years. Once limited to producing smaller craft, airfields are now retrofitted to manufacture everything from the sleek MiG Fighters to the massive Kirov Airships. Today, Soviet air superiority arguably rivals that of the Allied nations."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETAKULADESC
	"AKULA SUB - Invisible to enemy radar while submerged, Soviet Akula Subs lurk undersea in search of enemy ships. Although they must surface to fire, they are powerful enough to assault larger vessels directly."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETCHERDENKODESC
	"PREMIER ANATOLY CHERDENKO - Longtime leader of the Soviet Union, who has led the Union in an age of prosperity and military superiority. Once a famous theoretician, he rose to power meteorically even as Soviet forces under his advisement achieved victory after victory against their enemies the Allies."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETDASHADESC
	"INFORMATION OFFICER DASHA FEDOROVICH - Born to a poor family whose 10 children all willingly enlisted in the Soviet armed forces, Dasha was singled out as the most talented of the lot, so much so that Premier Cherdenko himself took notice of her. She now serves as an essential conduit between Soviet commanders across multiple fronts."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETIRONCURTAINDESC
	"IRON CURTAIN - The Iron Curtain is one of the Soviet military's most-feared creations. It gathers some sort of energy inside its furnace, which it uses to project a kinetic barrier onto armored forces. While the barrier lasts only a short while, affected targets are completely invulnerable during that time."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETKRUKOVDESC
	"GENERAL BORIS KRUKOV - Having fought and won countless battles against Allied forces, Krukov is a war hero in the eyes of the Soviet people. Those who know him personally, however, are more likely to be deathly afraid of getting on his bad side. He never could have achieved his status without being strict and without being ruthless."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETNATASHA01DESC
	"NATASHA VOLKOVA - Few know the true character of Natasha Volkova, the Union's legendary sniper, though her name and exploits are known across the world. A woman of few words, she is a seasoned professional--and, some would say, a cold-blooded killer. She deals with only the most urgent matters affecting the Union."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETNATASHA02DESC
	"NATASHA - So famous is this Soviet sniper-commando that her likeness is heavily used for purposes of military recruitment and propaganda. Some say she is hell-bent on living up to her living-legend image. She is extremely skilled with her custom rifle and has full authority to call airstrikes."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETTESLACOILDESC
	"TESLA COIL - The modern Soviet Tesla Coil is far different from the innocuous scientific device from which it takes its name. As one of the deadliest weapons developed at the Ministry of Experimental Science, this device can reduce a full-grown man to mere ash in just one tremendous electrical jolt."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETTHREEAPOCSDESC
	"The Soviets are virtually unchallenged on the ground, due to their exceptionally powerful and sturdy armor divisions. If only their Apocalypse Tanks could swim, say some Soviet political pundits, then surely the Union would have taken over all the world by now."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETZELINSKYDESC
	"DOCTOR GREGOR ZELINSKY - An ingenious and well-to-do scientist responsible for many popular Soviet household goods, a majority of which were appropriated by the Ministry of Experimental Science and eventually turned into weapons. A peaceful man by nature, Zelinsky is ambivalent about his current status as Union's top military scientist."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETZHANA2DESC
	"Faced with a new threat in the Empire of the Rising Sun, the Soviet military's publicity department worked tirelessly to produce high-impact propaganda with which to compel millions of young men into enlisting willingly. Pictured: Commander Zhana Agonskaya, posing for a Red Air Force recruitment campaign."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENWARRENDESC
	"COMMANDER WARREN FULLER - Not one for mincing words, Warren has survived numerous battles against the Soviets through regimented training, determination, and tenacity. Once captured by the Soviets, he fought his way to freedom with his bare hands. His men know he has a score to settle."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENZHANADESC
	"COMMANDER ZHANA AGONSKAYA - Men and women alike are conscripted into the Red Army, and Zhana distinguished herself almost immediately from among all the millions drafted as a brilliant pilot, good leader, and proud patriot. Now many of the Union's top aces seek transfer to her command."
End

ECS:STANDARDLOADSCREENTITLE
	"ESTABLISHING BATTLEFIELD CONTROL"
End

EregShortcutName
	"Electronic Registration"
End

