SUBTITLE:AFS10_11
	"*[61:3.1]Hello, and thank you all for coming.[66.5:3.5]I take this podium today reluctantly...[70.8:1.5]and with a heavy heart.[73.2:2.8]President Howard Ackerman was a great American.[76.4:4]I was proud to be his friend and proud to be his Vice President.[80.9:4.2]Yes, he did try to level Moscow and kill millions of innocent people,[85.6:2.6]but only because he was trying to protect us.[89.1:2.9]And in the end, isn't that what really matters?"
End

SUBTITLE:AFS10_12
	"*[93:5]We owe much to those brave heroes who stood against the forces of fascism and communism.[98.7:4.1]Like that courageous young commander who led the free world to victory.[102.7:2.2]Thank you commander...where ever you are.[106:6.5]Today, I will take the reigns of this great country and together we will march forward into a bright and prosperous future.[113.3:4.8]We will share with our defeated enemies the fruits of capitalism and consumerism."
End

SUBTITLE:AFS10_13
	"*[118.9:6.9]For if they're shopping for cars and plasma TVs, they won't want to build up massive armies or invent new weapons of war.[126.2:2.4]They'll be enjoying the American dream,[129.2:2.3]sitting with their families on Super Sunday,[132:2.4]watching the big game with the rest of us.[135.6:3.6]Fellow citizens, I humbly accept this honor[139.6:2.7]and promise to make you proud.[143.1:1.4]Thank you...[144.8:2.4]and God Bless America."
End

